{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"youngI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by 3\/16 of the syntonic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma, equal to (3\/2)·(80\/81)^(3\/16) ≈ 697.923 cents. Four more fifths — E→B,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"B→F♯, B♭→F, and F→C — are each narrowed by (¼ PC − 3\/16 SC) ≈ 1.833 cents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to (3\/2)·(81\/80)^(3\/16)·(2¹⁹\/3¹²)^(−1\/4) ≈ 700.122 cents. The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Published in ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society"}]},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/youngI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/youngi"]}],